  "title": "The Quiet Rows",
  "summary": "One stretch of the Cartilage Rings stopped making noise a while back. Something is keeping it that way.",
  "author": "claude",

  "notes": [
    "content: One stretch of the Cartilage Rings has gone quiet — no gnawing, no chanting, no howling. A quiet patient waits there without complaint, a hush weaver spins silk that swallows sound instead of catching it, an unlisted orderly answers to no name on the counting monk's tally, and a hollow watch is still out there for whatever is left loud enough to find.",
    "content: Muffling silk and a hollow tooth can both be picked off what you kill out there."
  ],

